# Build-context hygiene (2026-10-10, alongside the interpreter pin). The image needs the
# source tree, prompts/, static/ and .git/HEAD + .git/refs (db_write.git_sha reads them;
# there is no git binary in the image), nothing below. data/ is hidden by the
# fpl_model_data volume at /app/data in every service, the Windows venv is useless in a
# Linux image, and .git/objects is the repo's whole history.
.venv/
data/
.git/objects/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
eval/agent_evals/results/
# gitignored, laptop-only working dirs (never in the server tree; 851 MB of them on 2026-10-10)
fplcache/
tmp/
backups/
mlartifacts/
# secrets never in the image (2026-10-10): compose gives both services built from this image
# (fpl-copilot and fpl-scheduler) env_file: .env, and the scheduler bind-mounts the live file for
# the two scripts that parse it by path. Until now `COPY . .` baked the keys into every image.
.env
.env.*
